s to I  don't know any other way to say it  appears  to have murdered a journalist named  jamal Khashoggi inside the Saudi  consulate in Istanbul Turkey or in some  place which he was brought to secretly  or covertly in some way shape or form  jamal Khashoggi was a big critic of  Saudi Arabia  he was an American resident but not a  citizen which some have chosen to focus  on including Donald Trump and we'll talk  about that in a little bit and Khashoggi  disappeared on October 2nd after  visiting the Saudi consulate in Turkey  in Istanbul Turkey and this  understandably hit a nerve with many  people both individuals and governments  have started to say something about this  my twitter feed over the weekend was  filled with individuals saying things  like for example Andrew Ross Sorkin who  was scheduled to participate in an event  in Riyadh who says he's not going  because of this incident but then more  importantly I would argue countries have  actually said wait a second this is  insane and maybe it's time for sanctions  as an example we had 22 American  senators who pushed for an investigation  into the possibility of sanctioning  economically Saudi Arabia over this  incident and this was immediately bad  for Saudi Arabia Saudi Arabia's stock  market dropped as much as 7% biggest  drop since 2014 lost 33 billion in value  last week a shaky start already this  week so this is having an impact in  Saudi Arabia and Saudi Arabia  immediately threatens to retaliate to  any possible economic sanctions  according to their news news agency  s.p.a  basically saying we will screw the world  if you do this a quote attributed to an  official Saudi source by the s.p.a the  kingdom affirms its total rejection of  any threats and attempts to undermine it  whether by threatening to impose  economic sanctions using political  pressures or repeating false accusations  the kingdom also affirms that if it  receives any action it will respond with  greater action and that the kingdom